# v0.1.0

# Release v0.1.0

- Generation reliability improved with loop detection and contract-aware caps
- Installed binaries now include branch and commit provenance for traceability
- Project budget caps (max_tokens and other named limits) are enforced on runs
- Chat retains an uncapped wallclock budget even after project settings are merged
- Advisor is configurable and receives relevant project documents for better context
- Webhook notifications for important run state changes
- Overrides for ducklings, mode, and agent_turns available in stage_start and bug_triage
- Reopen action surfaced for fixed bugs and accepted tasks
- Test redo/relaunch requires a note and creates an audit entry for traceability
- Working tree is restored when aborting paused or failed builds
- Recovery controls (Clean or Commit) available when retire-test errors occur
- All valid abort and reject actions are visible on paused run cards
- Bugs are only marked as fixed after an accepted BUILD run, improving status reliability

## What shipped

### M-001

- **T-001** Expose budget lifting through MCP and identify the invalid kind field in lift errors (`b28cc5a`)
- **T-002** Detect token repetition loops and apply contract-aware generation caps (`55cae85`)
- **T-003** Always include next_steps in MCP status response, even when empty (`02d8bdd`)
- **T-004** Add per-project document lifecycle state to MCP status response (`432adc4`)
- **T-005** Expose reviewer findings and filing action through MCP run tools (`02aca83`)
- **T-006** Surface accepted-unreleased work and stamp installed binaries with branch and commit provenance (`80d63e5`)
- **T-007** Align MCP status unreleased branch fields with the OpenAPI contract (`485830c`)
- **T-008** Apply project budget max_tokens and other named caps to runs (`a038312`)
- **T-009** Only mark bugs fixed after an accepted BUILD run (`21c0449`)
- **T-010** Preserve an uncapped wallclock budget for chat after merging project settings (`04b37b5`)
- **T-011** Govern advisor replies through contract validation and record advice failures or timeouts (`d59130a`)
- **T-012** Add a configurable advisor seat and pass relevant project documents to advisor prompts (`6e5ecab`)
- **T-013** Emit webhook notifications for operator-relevant run transitions (`d909e3d`)
- **T-014** Add ducklings, mode, and agent_turns overrides to stage_start and bug_triage (`b61c1f3`)
- **T-015** Write .gitattributes with union merge rules at project init (`89aa838`)
- **T-016** Surface a discoverable Reopen action for fixed bugs and accepted tasks (`5b990a0`)
- **T-017** Orchestrate safe test-first redo/relaunch with a required note and an audit entry (`c7aa164`)
- **T-018** Retire-test cleanup path and a cap on redo commits per task (`2766f49`)
- **T-019** Restore the working tree when aborting a paused or failed build (`49fdb1c`)
- **T-020** Add actionable Clean or Commit recovery controls to the retire-test error state (`c942214`)
- **T-021** Expose every legal abort and reject action on paused run cards (`6c4f9b8`)
- **T-022** Include blocked reasons in MCP task_list rows (`a174617`)

